{
  "name": "Find work emails for a Google Sheet in bulk with LeadMagic",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Bulk work-email finder for Google Sheets\n\n### How it works\n1. Reads every row of your sheet.\n2. Skips rows that already have an email or lack a name and company.\n3. Finds each work email with LeadMagic in small, paced batches.\n4. Writes the email, status, and email provider back to the same row. Errors are written too, so nothing silently disappears.\n\nRerun it any time: finished rows are skipped, so it resumes where it stopped.\n\n### Setup\n1. Sheet columns: `First Name`, `Last Name`, `Company Domain`, `Company Name`, `Email`, `Email Status`, `Email Provider`, `Checked At`.\n2. Paste the sheet URL into **Read rows** and **Write result to row**.\n3. Select your Google Sheets and LeadMagic credentials.\n\n### Customization\nBatch size 5 plus a 1-second wait stays under the 300 requests per minute Email Finder limit on every plan. Raise the batch size on Growth (600/min) or higher plans.\n\nRequires the [LeadMagic community node](https://github.com/LeadMagic/leadmagic-n8n#install) (`n8n-nodes-leadmagic`). Tested with n8n 2.47 and n8n-nodes-leadmagic 1.8.0.",
        "height": 620,
        "width": 460
      },
      "id": "0a0990bf-ce0d-5e8a-8dcb-d1658ddee963",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -560,
        -320
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {},
      "id": "1a6b893e-607d-5adc-a57f-37ff95d065de",
      "name": "Run manually",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.manualTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        0,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
